# Keep shell scripts LF so they run inside Linux containers, even when edited on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Same for the browser code, because a test reads it as text and asserts on its shape.
# trail's "it all runs in begin()" test matches `\n  begin();\n}`, which CRLF breaks. The
# Linux runners check out LF and pass either way; this is what stops a Windows clone from
# failing a test that has nothing wrong with it.
*.js text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
# Normalize line endings for common text files; let Git auto-detect the rest.
* text=auto
